there's a problem here  doctor strange in the multiverse of  madness while it's actually a really  great movie has several pretty  noticeable issues including certain  cameos unanswered questions and one big  glaring issue that a lot of marvel  movies have started to fall into but  before we get into it spoiler alert for  doctor strange 2 since we'll be going  over all the spoilers in the movie as  well as the pretty scary horror scenes  in the film but first let's start with  the movie's opening scene  [Music]  the first issue with the multiverse of  madness was the really cold opening  scene we got absolutely no introduction  to the characters on screen the  alternate defender strange in america  chavez while i usually like a cold open  like you might see in the office i don't  feel like this cold open was done very  well it was like it was simply there in  an effort to shorten the film's run time  leaving very little time for setting up  the plot of the film one thing i did  like about the beginning of the film was  at the reception for christine's wedding  when strange turned her water into wine  just like the story of jesus turning  water into wine during the wedding at  cana after the big monster battle though  we were sent right into wanda's  introduction to the film and dr  strange's first conversation with wanda  seemed really unnatural there were lots  of badly placed cuts in their  conversation making it seem like their  dialogue was just unrealistic kind of  like a soap opera or an old sitcom the  next issue lies in the character cameos  in the film professor xavier captain  carter reed richards and black bolt of  the multiversal illuminati were pretty  much wasted these actors and the  characters they portrayed had so much  potential to add to the movie but their  time in the film was cut really short by  wanda john krasinski as reed richards or  mr fantastic for instance had so much  potential to act as a leading character  in the movie but wanda just turned him  into rubber bands with the little  expecto patronum and ended his time in  the film while their cameos were  basically wasted i actually really  enjoyed their death scenes it was just  so unexpected that all of them would die  so quickly it reminded me of the  completely unexpected scene in the tv  show invincible where omniman killed all  the guardians of the globe also just  because they're dead in this universe it  doesn't mean we won't see them again in  an alternate universe so we may still  get to see john krasinski again in the  fantastic four the biggest issue with  the movie though lies in an issue that  we've started to see in a lot of marvel  films which is that we don't ever get a  grounded friendly neighborhood conflict  anymore instead we get world-ending  events global conflicts or alien  invasions and when that's not enough we  get multiversal threats and universe  ending events like in doctor strange 2.  i miss the times when we simply got to  see a guy build a metal suit in a cave  so he can escape  instead we get a crazy witch trying to  steal the powers from a girl who can  travel the multiverse so she can be with  their non-kid kids or destroy the  multiverse trying because the mcu has  been around for so long and is getting  so large they feel like they have to  constantly one-up whatever happened in  the last movie marvel needs to realize  that not every movie can be end game  they can't all have world ending events  and still make audiences feel a high  level of character investment because we  typically know that everything will turn  out okay in the end also it seemed like  they were trying to shove just too much  into one movie we were left with a lot  of unanswered questions such as where  did america chavez come from or where  did she get her powers and we also just  had the bomb dropped on us that our  dreams are visions into our multiversal  selves lives it just didn't make much  sense and it left us with more questions  than answers also what was up with  doctor strange's third eye my only guess  is that it's a symbol of cathon  possessing doctor strange after he used  the darkhold since cathon is the one who  created the darkhold and gave the  scarlet witch her powers lastly the  after credit scenes were a bit of a  letdown we got a short scene of clia one  of doctor strange's love interests in  the comics inviting strange to join her  on a multiversal adventure to save a  universe from an incursion we also got a  scene of pizza papa played by bruce  campbell who makes an appearance in  almost every sam raimi film finally  stopping hitting himself in the face  before telling the audience it's over i  hope that these end credit scenes would  further connect the movie to loki or  spiderman no way home since that was  where we got to see the beginning of the  fracture of the multiverse so it was a  bit disappointing to not get this  connection i will say though that the  multiverse of madness had a ton of  amazing qualities the first thing that  stood out to me was that it took on the  persona of a horror film the first of  its kind in the mcu it was given what i  would call the raimi effect and what  exactly do i mean by the raimi effect  sam raimi the director for doctor  strange 2 has a very particular style  for his films he's known for directing  the original spider-man trilogy and the  evil dead franchise so he's no stranger  to superhero or horror films and i feel  like this movie put together some of the  best aspects of both genres to make one  great film it was fun to see tropes from  both the horror genre as well as the  superhero genre all in one movie like  how wonder would attack the protagonist  through mirrors or how the faces in the  pictures would turn to look at you as  you walk by we also got a classic fourth  wall break from wanda similar to the  ones we got in one division also i love  how we got an exorcist inspired wanda  after she exited the mirror dimension it  was so twisted and strange pun intended  that it made my hair stand on end and of  course in evil dead fashion we had to  get a zombie in the movie another thing  that really stood out to me was the  inclusion of transitions that are  completely characteristic of sam raimi's  work like we saw in his spider-man  trilogy as well as a striking music  composition which usually accompanies  any raimi movie the film's composer  danny elfman is well known for his  unique compositions and he's worked with  sam raimi multiple times in the past the  electric guitar riffs and rock and roll  music mixed in with the classical score  really set the tone for the film as one  that's completely different from the  other mcu films the one scene in  particular where this was the most  evident was when doctor strange was  fighting one of his multiversal selves  in a crazy fun musical battle that ended  with the multiversal strange getting  impaled this scene while it had a pretty  morbid ending actually reminded me of  fantasia the 1940 animated musical  anthology film by walt disney  productions the way the music interacted  physically with the characters and their  surroundings perfectly encapsulated the  effects present in fantasia doctor  strange in the multiverse of madness has  to be the craziest marvel movie we've  gotten to date even superseding the  craziness of avengers end game and  infinity war although it had several  issues such as the wasted cameos  unanswered questions and the unnecessary  one-upsmanship marvel movies seemed to  have always trying to top the last  world-ending event doctor strange 2 was  still an absolutely amazing film and i  can't wait to see where the marvel  multiverse will take us next anyways  that's gonna be all for today if you  like what you saw check out the video on  your screen for some different content  or drop a comment below on something  else you'd like to see also don't forget  to like and subscribe as it truly does  help me out and thanks for watching  rocket riley
 

